WEBVTT

00:02:28.644 --> 00:02:32.356
or as I like to think of it,
and maybe you, too,

00:02:32.356 --> 00:02:34.025
common-sense budgeting.

00:02:34.066 --> 00:02:35.401
(Laughter)

00:02:35.443 --> 00:02:37.320
So, I'm an economist,

00:02:37.361 --> 00:02:40.281
I work with public finance,
so public finance and budgets,

00:02:40.323 --> 00:02:44.869
but my specialty is helping governments
inject a gender perspective

00:02:44.869 --> 00:02:47.622
in their financial decisions and budgets.

00:02:48.122 --> 00:02:51.250
OK, so budgets are fairly simple,
straightforward,

00:02:51.292 --> 00:02:52.835
as it was introduced,

00:02:52.877 --> 00:02:54.128
and now, you are thinking,

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:56.505
"Well, that does not look
fairly straightforward."

00:02:56.547 --> 00:02:59.133
And it's intentionally done like that,

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:02.511
because this is how we often imagine
the budget to be: so complex,